    "created_at": "2016-11-03T11:08:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-03T11:08:08Z",
    "body": "I still think we should do what we can to prevent people from accidentally using SRI on things that don't work today but we would like to work tomorrow. If it doesn't work today, it is an authoring mistake to specify the attribute, and conformance checkers should give an error. If we don't do this, people will cargo-cult or test it and forget to remove when it doesn't do anything, and then we won't be able to add UA processing for `integrity` on e.g. module scripts.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
