    "created_at": "2019-02-19T03:04:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-02-19T03:12:35Z",
    "body": "> Element `script` must not have attribute `integrity` unless attribute `src` is also specified.\r\n\r\nI just implemented SRI on my inline scripts and the [markup validation service](https://validator.w3.org) throws the above. I don't know what \"Fallout from  https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1984\" means exactly but throwing on inline scripts with `integrity` feels like a mistake as it leads the implementation and reduces the value of SRI. Why was this added? I don't personally feel it should be there.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/alice/html/commit/84105175018d9611519a26adea74bdd0c150a524",
    "author_association": "NONE",
